{"evidence":["`crates/tank_core/src/conversions.rs:1-148` adds named NO3/NO2/NH4/NH3/PO4 factors plus bidirectional helpers, and `cargo test -p tank_core conversions --lib` passed all 7 conversion tests.","`crates/tank_core/src/types/snapshot.rs:16-28` and `crates/tank_api/src/handlers/snapshot.rs:13-26` rename the chemistry fields to basis-explicit names and rename TDS/conductivity to explicit estimate fields.","`crates/tank_tui/src/screens/chemistry.rs:23-59` correctly labels the dedicated chemistry screen with `mg N/L`, `mg P/L`, `mg C/L`, `GH (Ca+Mg)`, `KH (alkalinity)`, and `Est. TDS (7-ion)`.","`cargo check -p tank_tui` and `cargo check -p tank_api` both succeeded; `cargo test -p tank_core --test events` and `cargo test -p tank_core --test determinism` both passed.","Validation is partially blocked by an unrelated pre-existing test compile failure: `cargo test -p tank_core --test chemistry nh3_speciation_matches_reference_formula` fails at `crates/tank_core/tests/chemistry.rs:17` because `AnimalState.adults_count` no longer exists.","`rg -n \"serde\\(alias|serde\\(rename\" crates/tank_core/src/types/snapshot.rs crates/tank_api/src/handlers/snapshot.rs` returned no matches, so the renamed snapshot/API fields have no transition shim."],"findings_or_gaps":["`crates/tank_core/src/systems/events.rs:18-34` still emits `Free ammonia reached ... mg/L` and `Nitrite reached ... mg/L`. Those summaries are shown directly in the log UI via `crates/tank_tui/src/screens/log.rs:13-37` and returned by `/events` via `crates/tank_api/src/handlers/events.rs:12-21`, so users still see ambiguous chemistry units on surfaced API/UI paths.","`crates/tank_tui/src/screens/overview.rs:48-50` still compresses the derived chemistry row to `GH ... KH ... Est.TDS ...` without units, the `7-ion` qualifier, or the GH/KH derivation labels. The dedicated chemistry screen was fixed, but the overview screen still fails the acceptance criterion that surfaced metrics explain what is being shown.","The snapshot/API rename is a breaking wire-format change with no compatibility handling. `TankSnapshot` now serializes only the new field names in `crates/tank_core/src/types/snapshot.rs:9-28`, while `/snapshot` and `/snapshot/chemistry` stay on the same routes in `crates/tank_api/src/routes.rs:11-15`; existing consumers expecting `tan_mg_l`, `tds_mg_l`, etc. will break immediately."],"follow_up_or_amendments":["Update all user-visible chemistry copy paths, not just the main chemistry screen: change `SimEvent.summary` strings to explicit bases such as `mg NH3-N/L` and `mg N/L`, and add regression coverage in `crates/tank_core/tests/events.rs` for the rendered summaries.","Bring `crates/tank_tui/src/screens/overview.rs` into line with the chemistry screen by restoring units and derivation/estimate qualifiers, e.g. `GH (Ca+Mg)`, `KH (alkalinity)`, and `Est. TDS (7-ion) ... mg/L`.","Add a compatibility plan for the renamed snapshot/API fields before merge: either transitional `serde(alias)` support on the renamed fields, or a versioned endpoint/schema bump plus explicit migration notes/tests for downstream clients."],"outcome":"request_changes"}